<Group labelreference="L124" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">In this case, <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">dsolve</Font> returns the solution for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYnLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiYUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1JKG1mZW5jZWRHRiQ2JC1GIzYmLUYsNiVRInRGJ0YvRjIvJStleGVjdXRhYmxlR1EmZmFsc2VGJy8lMGZvbnRfc3R5bGVfbmFtZUdRJ05vcm1hbEYnL0YzUSdub3JtYWxGJ0ZDRj1GQEZD">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYnLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiYUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1JKG1mZW5jZWRHRiQ2JC1GIzYmLUYsNiVRInRGJ0YvRjIvJStleGVjdXRhYmxlR1EmZmFsc2VGJy8lMGZvbnRfc3R5bGVfbmFtZUdRJ05vcm1hbEYnL0YzUSdub3JtYWxGJ0ZDRj1GQEZD</Equation> explicitly with two arbitrary constants <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>. You can generate a plot of the solution for certain choices of parameters by using the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">subs</Font> command.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L125" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">gnat := subs(omega = 2, Gamma = 0.2, c__1 = 1, c__2 = 0, rhs(sol));
plot([Re(gnat), Im(gnat)], t = 0..10);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSVnbmF0R0YoLUkkZXhwR0YlNiMqJl4kJCEiIyEiIiQiK3VbKCoqKT4hIioiIiJJInRHRihGOTcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="Maple Plot" layout="Maple Plot"><Plot height="500.0" originalheight="500.0" type="two-dimensional" width="500.0" originalwidth="500.0" plot-scale="1.0" plot-xtrans="0.0" plot-ytrans="0.0" gridlinevisibility="1" legendvisibility="false" input="_ATTRIBUTE(&quot;input&quot; = [TABLE([1 = plot, 2 = [Re(exp((-.2+1.989974874*I)*t)), Im(exp((-.2+1.989974874*I)*t))], 3 = (t = 0 .. 10)]), &quot;originalview&quot; = [0. .. 10., -.732908476788185714 .. 1.], &quot;originalaxesticks&quot; = AXESTICKS(DEFAULT, DEFAULT, _ATTRIBUTE(&quot;source&quot; = &quot;mathdefault&quot;))])"></Plot></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L260" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Notice that the solution was complex. We can get the purely real solution by solving the ODE with some initial conditions specified.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L261" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">ics := a(0) = 1, D(a)(0) = sqrt(2);
sol := dsolve({ode, ics});</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSRpY3NHRig2JC8tSSJhR0YoNiMiIiEiIiIvLS1JIkRHRiU2I0YxRjIqJCIiIyNGNEY7NyRGL0Y1</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L320" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Now, the solution involves no arbitrary constants, and one can confirm that the ODE and the initial conditions are satisfied:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L321" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">simplify(subs(sol, ode));
simplify(subs(t = 0, sol));
diff(sol, t);
simplify(subs(t = 0, rhs(%)));</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEiMEYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">IiIh</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">Ly1JImFHNiI2IyIiISIiIg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkmbXNxcnRHNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2Iy1JI21uR0YkNiRRIjJGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">KiQiIiMjIiIiRiM=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L380" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">To get <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">dsolve</Font> to solve a coupled system, put the equations in a set:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L381" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">ode1 := diff(u(x), x, x)-v(x) = 0;
ode2 := diff(v(x), x, x)+u(x)+2*v(x) = 0;
sol1 := dsolve({ode1, ode2});</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSVvZGUxR0YoLywmLUklZGlmZkdGJjYkLUkidUdGKDYjSSJ4R0YoLUkiJEdGJjYkRjYiIiMiIiItSSJ2R0YoRjUhIiIiIiE3Iy8sJi1GMTYkLUYxNiRGM0Y2RjZGO0Y8Rj5GPw==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSVvZGUyR0YoLywoLUklZGlmZkdGJjYkLUkidkdGKDYjSSJ4R0YoLUkiJEdGJjYkRjYiIiMiIiItSSJ1R0YoRjVGO0YzRjoiIiE3Iy8sKC1GMTYkLUYxNiRGM0Y2RjZGO0Y8RjtGM0Y6Rj4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L382" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">To include the initial conditions, just make the set bigger (with the initial conditions).</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L383" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">ic1 := u(0) = 3, D(u)(0) = 0;
ic2 := v(0) = 0, D(v)(0) = 0;
[ode1, ode2, ic1, ic2];
sol2 := dsolve([ode1, ode2, ic1, ic2]);
U := subs(sol2, u(x));
V := subs(sol2, v(x));
plot([U, V], x = -4..4, axes = boxed);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSRpYzFHRig2JC8tSSJ1R0YoNiMiIiEiIiQvLS1JIkRHRiU2I0YxRjJGMzckRi9GNQ==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSRpYzJHRig2JC8tSSJ2R0YoNiMiIiFGMy8tLUkiREdGJTYjRjFGMkYzNyRGL0Y0</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSVzb2wyR0YoPCQvLUkidUdGKDYjSSJ4R0YoLCYtSSRjb3NHRiVGMiIiJComLUkkc2luR0YlRjIiIiJGM0Y7I0Y3IiIjLy1JInZHRihGMiwkRjgjISIkRj03I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJVR0YoLCYtSSRjb3NHRiU2I0kieEdGKCIiJComLUkkc2luR0YlRjEiIiJGMkY3I0YzIiIjNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJWR0YoLCQqJi1JJHNpbkdGJTYjSSJ4R0YoIiIiRjNGNCMhIiQiIiM3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="Maple Plot" layout="Maple Plot"><Plot height="500.0" originalheight="500.0" type="two-dimensional" width="500.0" originalwidth="500.0" plot-scale="1.0" plot-xtrans="0.0" plot-ytrans="0.0" gridlinevisibility="1" legendvisibility="false" input="_ATTRIBUTE(&quot;input&quot; = [TABLE([1 = plot, 2 = [3*cos(x)+(3/2)*sin(x)*x, -(3/2)*sin(x)*x], 3 = (x = -4 .. 4), 4 = (axes = boxed)]), &quot;originalview&quot; = [-3.97999999998137355 .. 3.97999999998137355, -6.44511127150379437 .. 4.43916745940219037], &quot;originalaxesticks&quot; = AXESTICKS(DEFAULT, DEFAULT, _ATTRIBUTE(&quot;source&quot; = &quot;mathdefault&quot;))])"></Plot></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 1" layout="Heading 1">Solving differential equations numerically</Text-field></Title>
<Group labelreference="L408" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">restart;</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L411" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">There are many examples of differential equations that Maple cannot solve analytically. In these cases, a default call to <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">dsolve</Font> returns a null (blank) result:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L412" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">ode := diff(y(x), x, x)+y(x)^2 = x^2;
dsolve(ode);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSRvZGVHRigvLCYtSSVkaWZmR0YmNiQtSSJ5R0YoNiNJInhHRigtSSIkR0YmNiRGNiIiIyIiIiokRjNGOkY7KiRGNkY6NyMvLCYtRjE2JC1GMTYkRjNGNkY2RjtGPEY7Rj0=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L413" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">If this happens, one can obtain a solution numerically by specifying initial conditions and providing the option &quot;numeric&quot;:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L414" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">ICs := y(0) = 0, D(y)(0) = 1/2;
sol := dsolve({ode, ICs}, numeric);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSRJQ3NHRig2JC8tSSJ5R0YoNiMiIiFGMy8tLUkiREdGJTYjRjFGMiMiIiIiIiM3JEYvRjQ=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L415" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The output of <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">dsolve</Font> is by default a Maple procedure of a single argument. If we call this procedure with argument <Font italic="true">x</Font>, we obtain information about the solution at that value of the independent variable:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L416" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">sol(1);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM3JS9JInhHRigkIiIiIiIhLy1JInlHRig2I0YuJCIwbScqWyg+Jyk0YyEjOi8tSSVkaWZmR0YmNiRGM0YuJCIwbmJKPUFMUihGODcjNyVGLS9GM10zRkUxRjM5OTUzNzczNzY5L0Y6XTNGRTdBODlDMEE1MTZDN0E=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L417" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">That is, we get a list giving us a numeric approximation to the value of the unknown and its first derivative at our choice of <Font italic="true">x</Font>. If the equation we wanted to solve was higher order (say, <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>th order), we would have more elements in the list corresponding to all the derivatives of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy8lK2V4ZWN1dGFibGVHUSZmYWxzZUYnL0YzUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy8lK2V4ZWN1dGFibGVHUSZmYWxzZUYnL0YzUSdub3JtYWxGJw==</Equation> up to <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>th order. The default behaviour of <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">dsolve</Font>/<Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">numeric</Font> is to return a procedure that itself returns a list; however, we can instead have it return a list of procedures by using the optional command &quot;output = listprocedure.&quot;</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L418" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">sol := dsolve({ode, ICs}, numeric, output = listprocedure);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L419" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Here, we get a list of three equations. The RHS of each equation is a procedure that calculates what is represented on the LHS. For example, the RHS of the second element is a procedure that calculates <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYmLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1JKG1mZW5jZWRHRiQ2JC1GIzYlLUYsNiVRInhGJ0YvRjIvJStleGVjdXRhYmxlR1EmZmFsc2VGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRidGQEY9RkA=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYmLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1JKG1mZW5jZWRHRiQ2JC1GIzYlLUYsNiVRInhGJ0YvRjIvJStleGVjdXRhYmxlR1EmZmFsc2VGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRidGQEY9RkA=</Equation>. We can isolate this particular procedure as follows:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L420" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">y_sol := sol[2];
y_sol := rhs(y_sol);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L423" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Now, <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">y_sol</Font> is a procedure that just returns the numeric solution for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy8lK2V4ZWN1dGFibGVHUSZmYWxzZUYnL0YzUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy8lK2V4ZWN1dGFibGVHUSZmYWxzZUYnL0YzUSdub3JtYWxGJw==</Equation> as a function of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy8lK2V4ZWN1dGFibGVHUSZmYWxzZUYnL0YzUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy8lK2V4ZWN1dGFibGVHUSZmYWxzZUYnL0YzUSdub3JtYWxGJw==</Equation>:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L424" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">y_sol(2);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFExMS43OTI3OTEwNDAwOTk4MkYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyMkIjAjKSo0UzV6I3oiISM5NyNdM0ZGQ0FGNDVBODVDQTYyRQ==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L425" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">This procedure can readily be used to obtain a plot of the numeric solution of the ODE:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L426" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">plot(y_sol(x), x = -10..10, axes = boxed);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="Maple Plot" layout="Maple Plot"><Plot height="500.0" originalheight="500.0" type="two-dimensional" width="500.0" originalwidth="500.0" plot-scale="1.0" plot-xtrans="0.0" plot-ytrans="0.0" gridlinevisibility="1" legendvisibility="false" input="_ATTRIBUTE(&quot;input&quot; = [TABLE([1 = plot, 2 = [y_sol(x)], 3 = (x = -10 .. 10), 4 = (axes = boxed)]), &quot;originalview&quot; = [-10. .. 10., -.465245090190137489 .. 10.4270989691758924], &quot;originalaxesticks&quot; = AXESTICKS(DEFAULT, DEFAULT, _ATTRIBUTE(&quot;source&quot; = &quot;mathdefault&quot;))])"></Plot></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L433" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">This is not the only way to obtain a plot of the numeric solution of an ODE; look at <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">?plots</Font>/<Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">odeplot</Font> for an alternate method (I recommend the one given here, however). The <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">dsolve</Font>/<Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">numeric</Font> command can also be used to solve systems of ODEs, such as the following (this is a predator-prey model from mathematical biology where <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>and <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYmLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiWUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1JKG1mZW5jZWRHRiQ2JC1GIzYlLUYsNiVRIlRGJ0YvRjIvJStleGVjdXRhYmxlR1EmZmFsc2VGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRidGQEY9RkA=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYmLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiWUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1JKG1mZW5jZWRHRiQ2JC1GIzYlLUYsNiVRIlRGJ0YvRjIvJStleGVjdXRhYmxlR1EmZmFsc2VGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRidGQEY9RkA=</Equation>represent the populations of fish and humans, respectively):</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L434" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">ODE1 := diff(X(T), T) = -X(T)*(-1+Y(T));
ODE2 := diff(Y(T), T) = Y(T)*(-1+X(T))*alpha;</Text-field>
</Input>
